--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WEB SOURCE SHAPE (read end-to-end — covenant #3)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GrafanaPanelPage.tsx is a deterministic Grafana-panel-builder. `usePageTitle('Grafana Panel
Builder')` + a `space-y-6 p-6` container holding, in order:
  1. PageTitle (powerGrafana.title) + intro paragraph (powerGrafana.intro).
  2. `<AINLGrafanaPanel onApply={handleApplyAiDraft} />` — the propose-only Helix
     natural-language drafter (its OWN P4 parity unit, shared-surfaces/AINLGrafanaPanel,
     already DONE — 9 Apple files). `onApply` pretty-prints the proposed panel into the
     editor via `JSON.stringify(draft.panel, null, 2)`; the browser/app NEVER pushes to Grafana.
  3. GlassPanel1 — the manual JSON editor: PanelTitle (editor.title), a Textarea
     (placeholder + aria-label editor.label), and Copy (editor.copy) / Clear (editor.clear)
     actions gated on `canCopy`, plus the transient `statusMessage` (editor.copyEmpty /
     copyUnavailable / copySuccess / copyFailed).
  4. GlassPanel2 — curated panel types (panelTypes.title/intro) — 8 entries, sorted localeCompare.
  5. GlassPanel3 — curated datasource types (datasourceTypes.title/intro) — 2 entries w/ UIDs.
  6. GlassPanel4 — curated table catalog (tables.title/intro) — 5 postgres tables w/ columns.
The three `CURATED_*` arrays are install-wide-static data the page inlines (rendered WITHOUT
`t()`); `panelJson` persists to localStorage so a long edit survives navigation. The manifest
record (apps/parity/parity-manifest.json id=page:power-user/GrafanaPanel) extracts the 4 named
GlassPanels, the single `success` data state (NO API dataSources — renders from local/nav state),
and 17 i18n strings (requiredCount=22 = 4 panels + 1 state + 17 strings).

