OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/PowerUser/**`. That path
does NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group (the app targets list `Sources`
+ `TeslaSync/{widget-primitives,dashboard-widgets,feature-views,misc-surfaces,shared-surfaces}` —
there is no `TeslaSync/Features`). The repo's real, compiled canonical page home is
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Domain>/**` — where every sibling P7 page ships
(notifications/Webhooks, notifications/AuditLog, admin/ApiPlayground, …) and which `Sources`
already lists as a project.yml source path (createIntermediateGroups). The page therefore ships at
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/PowerUser/**`, the faithful equivalent of the prompt's
`Features/PowerUser`. Strings ship in the platform catalog
`apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This is the same reconciliation
the sibling notifications-Webhooks / notifications-AuditLog logs recorded.

ROUTE HOSTING: the web route `/power/grafana` is nested. A dedicated `.powerGrafana` AppRoute case
is added (pathSegment `power/grafana` → `.path` `/power/grafana` matching web exactly; System group
alongside `.powerUser`; SF Symbol `chart.xyaxis.line`), `AppRouteParser` aliases `/power/grafana`
→ `.powerGrafana` (REQUIRED — the generic first-segment fallback resolves `power`, which no route
owns, so it would otherwise return nil), and `GrafanaPanelRouteRegistration` hosts the page, chained
into `\.routeHosts` in TeslaSyncApp.swift after the Exports registration. The page is reachable via
the System-group sidebar entry and any `/power/grafana` deep link. (Navigation registration is an
allowed file per the prompt.)

